      "path": "experiments/bag-results/Bags/Rank.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "“Every ranking of `b` has the rows of `b`” would also hold if `rank` produced no ranking, while equality with `pure b` guarantees that at least one ranking exists. Fix: state that `rank le b` produces at least one ranking and that every ranking it produces has exactly the rows of `b`, including duplicates."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261128T140607Z-9e4281c5#2",
      "line": 37,
      "path": "experiments/bag-results/Bags/Arrange.lean",
      "rule": "R2",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The docstring requires entire rows to be identical, although `max(x)` returns the same value for tied rows `(id=1, x=5)` and `(id=2, x=5)`. Fix: state the condition on the returned aggregate values at the tied extremum."
    },
    {
      "id": "20261128T140607Z-9e4281c5#3",
      "line": 70,
      "path": "experiments/bag-results/Bags/Equivalence.lean",
      "rule": "R3",
      "severity": "should",
      "text": "The proof sketch says that each ranking of the second result has one row, although each has two rows in two singleton groups. Fix: say that the canonical form preserves both singleton groups in each ranking."
    }
